### CB-3 — No React Error Boundaries — Any Exception Crashes the App
**Issue:** Zero `ErrorBoundary` components in the codebase. Any unhandled React render error
or async error will unmount the entire application, showing a blank screen with no recovery path.
**Action:** Add a root-level ErrorBoundary in `src/App.tsx`:
```tsx
// src/components/layout/ErrorBoundary.tsx
class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component {
  state = { error: null };
  static getDerivedStateFromError(error) { return { error }; }
  componentDidCatch(error, info) { /* log to Sentry */ }
  render() {
    if (this.state.error) return <AppErrorScreen onRetry={() => this.setState({ error: null })} />;
    return this.props.children;
  }
}
```
Wrap each route cluster (Player, Coach, Parent) in its own boundary so one role's crash doesn't
affect others.

